Ok it's only a matter of how do we update the url, here's the same widget with code fixed:

```js
search.addWidget({
  container: document.querySelector('#custom-widget'),
  render: function(options) {
    var link = document.createElement('a');
    link.innerText = 'test';
    link.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      options.helper.toggleRefine('brand', 'Samsung');
      history.replaceState(null, '', location.search + '&isCustom=true&test_custom=false');
      options.helper.search();
    });
    this.container.innerHTML = '';
    this.container.appendChild(link);
  }
});
```

So basically, for anyone wondering, you need to do this to be able to add custom url attributes in the right way:

```js
      options.helper.toggleRefine('brand', 'Samsung');
      history.replaceState(null, '', location.search + '&isCustom=true&test_custom=false');
      options.helper.search();
```

In this particular order, using replaceState. Thanks @bobylito
